This is a smooth, fully turbulent, fixed-hull URANS prediction and has not been validated against experiments.

## Operating point and assumptions

- Fully submerged hull, centreline depth: {{ "%.3f"|format(depth_m) }} m
- Seawater: {{ "%.3f"|format(density) }} kg/m³, kinematic viscosity {{ "%.6g"|format(nu) }} m²/s
- Fixed hull at 0° pitch and yaw; relative flow along normalized +X
- Transient incompressible single-phase URANS, SST k-omega, smooth wall functions
- Second-order time integration; drag reported as an autocorrelation-aware time mean
- Cavitation value is a static-pressure screen; no multiphase cavitation model
- No free surface, appendages, propulsion, control-surface deflection, transition, roughness, manoeuvring, or experimental validation

